UseInterpolation -- use interpolation to find polynomials in the kernel of a map
********************************************************************************

Description
===========

This option is a boolean that allows one to specify if interpolation should be
used to find polynomials in each homogeneous component of $\ker(F)$. This
option is false by default. If it is set to false then *note computeComponent:
computeComponent, will be used to find polynomials in each homogeneous
component which is purely symbolic. If it is set to true then *note
interpolateComponent: interpolateComponent, will be used to to find polynomials
in each homogeneous component which are in the kernel with high probability.
Setting this option to true will often significantly speed up the computation
for large polynomial maps, especially in higher degree components.

Functions with optional argument named UseInterpolation:
========================================================

  * "componentsOfKernel(...,UseInterpolation=>...)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note UseInterpolation: UseInterpolation, is a *note symbol:
(Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

