File: MultigradedImplicitization.info, Node: UseMatroid, Prev: UseInterpolation, Up: Top

UseMatroid -- use the algebraic matroid of a polynomial map represented by the jacobian to skip computation of irrelevant components of the kernel
**************************************************************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

The option UseMatroid is a boolean that allows one to specify if the matroid
given by the jacobian should be used to automatically skip components. This
option is true by default. If it is set to false, then every homogeneous
component will be checked, even if it is impossible for a polynomial with the
necessary support to belong to the kernel. For very small examples, it may be
slightly faster to set this to false.

